    "architecture": "aarch64",
    "context": "Native musl ELF64 root/UID1000: 696 positioned-vector cases preserve complete pos_l, ignore native pos_h, reject signed negatives before malformed vector/descriptor errors, and reserve current-position -1 behavior for v2. Sparse data at 4 GiB + 123, 8 GiB - 1 (crossing 8 GiB), 8 GiB + 17 and lower 32-bit aliases are verified by scalar I/O, file size/blocks and cursor. Each unchanged cohort fails 60 raw offset cases, 144 negative cases and 14 sentinel cases; public musl wrappers already pass and remain preservation controls. Fixed cohorts pass all 348 cases each. Two 200-cycle valid/error/sentinel cohorts retain flat slab classes/big pages (321 ARM, 4258 x86); native range regressions remain flat. Eight guest cases and eight host tests pass; 62 input hashes verified. Existing 406 ARM/295 x86 allocation allowance failures are unchanged. GNU libc wrappers, native ELF32/translation, positioned header/descriptor lifetime, positive-offset error ordering, flags, MAX_RW_COUNT, shared-offset atomicity, disk-backed files and exhaustion remain separate qualification",
